ESP32-CAM validation
====================

The user requires newly created artifacts under ~/Desktop/Codex-projects/.
Host tests and the original working-source snapshot are therefore stored in:
  ~/Desktop/Codex-projects/esp-cam-validation/

Re-run:
  python3 ~/Desktop/Codex-projects/esp-cam-validation/run-checks.py

The runner regenerates its includes from current src files (hardware includes
and POSIX calls use test adapters), builds with AddressSanitizer/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer,
and exercises concurrent capture, slow consumers, Wi-Fi loss, SD/camera errors,
allocation/task failures, repeated sessions and network input/response limits.
It also runs actual embedded UI JavaScript and the FFmpeg export format check.

These host adapters are regression checks, not an ESP32 simulator. Follow the
on-board validation checklist in SERIAL_PROTOCOL.md before relying on recordings.
